From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Grische <github@grische.xyz>
Date: Thu, 13 Aug 2026 12:07:13 +0000
Subject: net: ethernet: lantiq: report the real dequeue port in the TX-init
 marker

The per-port marker at the end of ndo_open's TX-init step prints a literal
"(DMA2TX ch5)". That was written when eth0 was the only port that opened,
and ch5 is the eth0/GPHY5 path; now that all four LAN ports open it is
printed unchanged for eth1..eth3, where it is simply false.

Print port->cbm_deq_port instead, which is the value the rest of the TX
path actually keys off - hdma_port_enable(), hdma_port_disable() and the
CBM dequeue arithmetic all take it. Four boot lines that used to agree
with each other and disagree with the hardware now name the port each
netdev really dequeues from, which is the thing worth having in a boot
log.

Log text only; no functional change.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-fable-5
Signed-off-by: Grische <github@grische.xyz>

diff --git a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/intel_xrx500.c b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/intel_xrx500.c
index 5a2505a11d6f..ca44fa3a31dc 100644
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/intel_xrx500.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/lantiq/intel_xrx500.c
@@ -598,8 +598,8 @@ static int intel_xrx500_open_step4_tx(struct intel_xrx500_port *port)
 
 	port->state_tx_initialized = true;
 
-	pr_info("intel-xrx500: %s TX path CPU-ENQUEUE (DMA2TX ch5)\n",
-		netdev_name(port->netdev));
+	pr_info("intel-xrx500: %s TX path CPU-ENQUEUE (cbm_deq_port %u)\n",
+		netdev_name(port->netdev), port->cbm_deq_port);
 
 	return 0;
 }
